# __DATASET__ sample dataset

> Scenario description - what this dataset sets up and what it lets you demo / test.
> Approximate record counts per table. No client data: use generic / Contoso names.

## Tables (dependency order)

| # | CSV | Table | Records | Notes |
|---|-----|-------|---------|-------|
| 01 | `01_ContosoAccounts.csv` | `hso_contosoaccount` | n | parents |
| 02 | `02_ContosoContracts.csv` | `hso_contosocontract` | n | children -> accounts |

## Run

```powershell
# Seed (idempotent - safe to re-run)
.\Import-__DATASET__.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl https://yourorg.crm.dynamics.com/ -Interactive

# Validate without writing
.\Import-__DATASET__.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl https://yourorg.crm.dynamics.com/ -Interactive -DryRun

# Capture current state back into the CSVs (deterministic)
.\Export-__DATASET__.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl https://yourorg.crm.dynamics.com/ -Interactive

# Tear down (reverse order; safe to re-run)
.\Remove-__DATASET__.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl https://yourorg.crm.dynamics.com/ -Interactive
```

Authentication resolves in this order: `-AccessToken` -> `-Interactive` -> service principal
(`-ClientId`/`-ClientSecret` or `.claude/auth-settings.json`). Shared helpers come from the
repo-root `.scripts/Common-Functions.ps1` (provisioned by `hso-dataverse-init-repo`).

